## 2. Causality Assessment

**Suspected drug:** Amoxicillin
**Reported adverse reaction:** Skin rash

The patient developed a skin rash three days after starting amoxicillin. This establishes a reasonable temporal relationship between drug exposure and the adverse reaction.

The patient recovered after discontinuation of amoxicillin. This is a positive dechallenge, meaning the reaction improved after the suspected medicine was withdrawn.

However, the case does not provide sufficient information to exclude all alternative causes, such as the underlying illness or other medications. It also does not report whether the reaction recurred following re-exposure to amoxicillin.

